  "sourceUrl": "https://e.huawei.com/en/documents/others/621bfc22e8564cf69ae86581569a7594",
  "notes": "Port list is a stated card complement, not a fixed chassis figure: the E6616 is a 5U shelf with 14 service slots, so 56 client + 28 line is what \"14x B1LDCD\" means. Fewer boards, or the OTN/SDH switch boards (K5XCH 2.4T OTN, K5SXCH OTN+SDH) in place of a muxponder, give a different box - the same convention as devices/arista/7504r.json.\n\nPer board, B1LDCD is 4x 100GE client (QSFP28, LR4/SR4/CLR4 or OTU4) into 2x programmable 100G/200G line (CFP2). The line side is modelled at 200G in the simulator's 200G optical cage (qsfp56) because there is no CFP cage; the physical module is CFP2, so a lab planning optics should order CFP2, not QSFP56. Switching a board to its 100G line mode halves the line rate and lets 4x OTU4 map to 2x OTU4.\n\nNot a packet switch: client ports carry OTU4/100GE into OTN containers, and there is no L2/L3 forwarding, which is why capabilities is cli only - same reading as the Cisco NCS 1004. FEC, PRBS, ALS, 1588v2, G.8275.1 and AES-256 client encryption are board features and are not modelled as port capabilities."
}
